eceptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 07 16     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR KERATIN LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   The lymph nodes do not show keratin positive carcinoma cells  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 09 19 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are five specimens  Labeled  Left breast anterior  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm pink yellow fibroadipose tissue  entirely frozen as frozen section  1  now A  Labeled  Left breast lateral deep  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm pink yellow fibroadipose tissue  entirely frozen as frozen section  2  now B  Labeled  Left breast superior  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm pink yellow fibroadipose tissue  entirely frozen as frozen section  3  now C  Labeled  Left breast deep biopsy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm pink yellow fibroadipose tissue  entirely frozen as frozen section  4  now in D  Labeled  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm yellow fibroadipose ti