for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show moderate  2   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 15 05     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Right  block C   HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 to chromosome 17 signals in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 14 24 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with two localization wires in place  A short black stitch designates the superior margin and a long black stitch the lateral  The posterior margin is inked black  the anterior blue  the superior green  the inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm indurated  gray white  stellate mass which comes to 0 2cm of the posterior  the 0 3cm of the anterior  0 3cm of the superior  0 6cm of the anteromedial  0 9cm of the inferior  and 4 1cm of the lateral margins  The remaining cut surface shows predominately tan yellow adipose tissue  representative sections are submitted as follows  A D  Tumor mass submitted from lateral to medial  with radial sections at the medial margin and area designated by the localization wire as C  E F  Fibrous tissue surrounding second localization wire  submitted from lateral to medial  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary lymph node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue which is sectioned to reveal ten firm gray pink lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 7cm in greatest dimension  The lymph nodes are entirely submitted as G I  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast medial hemisphere final shave margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with two black stitches along one aspect  The stitched surface is inked black and the opposite surface is blue  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal areas of dense gray white  focally cystic fibrous tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted as J O  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast final shaved margin lateral hemisphere  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with a single black stitch along one aspect  The stitched aspect is inked black  the opposite surface blue  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a predominately tan yellow adipose cut surface  The specimen is entirely submitted as P R  Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  HEIKE VARNHOLT  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LYMPH NODE RIGHT AXILLA  DISSECTION PART C  BREAST RIGHT MEDIAL FINAL SHAVED MARGIN  EXCISION PART D  BREAST RIGHT LATERAL FINAL SHAVED MARGIN  EXCISION , 0.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  23 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 12 CLINICAL DATA  50 y o  female with carcinoma of the right breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  RE EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  FORMING SEVERAL NODULES ADJACENT TO THE BIOPSY CAVITY AND EXTENDING TO THE SUPERIOR AND INFERIOR MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN IN SEVERAL FOCI  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The invasive carcinoma probably aggregates to less than 1 0cm  BREAST  RIGHT   FINAL SHAVED MARGIN    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 3 OF 12 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  In 2 lymph nodes  the metastatic foci span less than 0 2cm  The tumor cells do not transgress the lymph node capsules  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 02                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 43 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast lumpectomy  is a oriented breast re excision specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm  with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm skin ellipse with a 2 0cm long well healed  oblique scar  The surgeon has denoted the superior aspect with a short stitch  and the lateral aspect with a long stitch  The superior half of the specimen is inked blue and the inferior half is inked black  Specimen is then sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm hemorrhagic area abutting the deep resection margin  In addition  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm rubbery  firm white area abutting close to the inferior half of the specimen  A poorly demarcated  white  rubbery  firm area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm lies at the deep aspect of the superior resection margin  This specimen is entirely submitted proceeding medially to laterally in cassettes A through E  with the described lesions in cassettes B  C and D  Received   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right final shaved margins  are four fragments of focally cauterized fibroadipose tissue measuring from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Since the specimen is received in four separate pieces  the specimen is sectioned and submitted entirely with the two smaller fragments in cassette F  the intermediate size fragment bisected in cassette G  the largest fragment serially sectioned in cassettes H and I  Received   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fragment of adipose tissue from which lymph nodes are dissected and submitted in cassettes J through P  Resident  JUSTIN M  CATES  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Simon Powell  M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   FINAL SHAVED MARGIN    EXCISION PART C  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION   report_end  , 3.
