sitive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 33 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and unit number  in three separate parts  Labeled  right breast  short superior  long lateral  is a 76 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm  breast lumpectomy specimen with an overlying 4 7cm  long and REMOVED_DATE wide skin ellipse that contains a centrally located  longitudinal  4 2cm  long  well healed scar  A short suture designates the superior margin  and a long suture designates the lateral margin  The specimen is inked in black entirely  and then double inked in blue on the anterior surface  red on the lateral surface  and yellow on the medial surface  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  hemorrhagic  oval biopsy cavity that is located 0 5cm  from the nearest medial margin  0 8cm  from the lateral margin  1 2cm  from the superior margin  1 2cm  from the inferior margin  0 3cm  from the deep margin  and 1 2cm  from the skin or anterior surface  The biopsy cavity is surrounded by focally white  shiny  rub