Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  28 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  28 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 11 CLINICAL DATA  33 year old lady with left breast infiltrating ductal carcinoma with intraductal component  Re excision      REVISED REPORT     Reason for Revision  CORRECTED INTRA OPERATIVE PATHOLOGIST Revised by  Teri L  Moore  MD Revised on 23 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 07 15                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   REEXCISION  FIBROSIS  FAT NECROSIS  AND FOREIGN BODY REACTION CONSISTENT WITH BIOPSY CAVITY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL MALIGNANCY  SEE NOTE  NOTE  There is marked chronic inflammation with fat necrosis and histiocytic reaction in the permanent slide made from the frozen section tissue  however  carcinoma is not seen  It is not possible to locate the frozen section slide to confirm the frozen section diagnosis of malignancy  and it is possible the fat necrosis with inflammation represents the area interpreted as malignant on frozen section  AXILLA  LEFT  NODES   EXCISION  2 of 19 LYMPH NODES POSITIVE FOR METASTATIC ADENOCARCINOMA  MICROMETASTASES   Diagnosis by  Teri L  Moore  MD Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 08 31                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm lumpectomy specimen with an overlying skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm with a central healed scar along its length  Two sutures designating the medial resection margin and one suture designating the superior resection margin are present  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1cm cavity that is lined by tan brown  shaggy surface  The cavity is 0 6cm from the medial resection margin  0 3cm from the inferior resection margin  0 6cm from the superior resection margin  1 9cm from the lateral resection margin and 1 6cm from the skin  A 0 5cm in greatest dimension  ill defined tan lesion is present just lateral to the cavity  Section Code  A  frozen section  1  B  medial resection margin  en face  C  cavity in relation to the superior resection margin  D  cavity in relation to the inferior resection margin  E  lateral resection margin en face  F    lesion  G M  90  of the cavity  N  the cavity in relation to the skin  O S  rest of the breast tissue  Also received fresh labeled  Left axilla nodes  is a 7 x 6 x 1cm piece of adipose tissue in which are found tan brown rubbery lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 5cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  entirely submitted in T through Y  Resident  Essam Ahmed  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS      LEFT  BREAST  1  RESIDUAL INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  2  FAT NECROSIS  3  THE INKED MARGIN IS FREE OF TUMOR  O R  Resident  C  Diana Jordan  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   AXILLA NODE  LEFT    report_end  , 2.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  13 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 18 51 CLINICAL DATA  49 year old female status post right modified radical mastectomy in  REMOVED_CASE_ID  with residual disease  now with left mammographic abnormality  read as infiltrating ductal carcinoma on needle biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL ADENOCARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  SEE NOTE  WITH EXTENSIVE LYMPHATIC VASCULAR INVASION AND MULTIFOCAL INVOLVEMENT OF THE BREAST  REMOVED_DATE AXILLARY LYMPH NODES ARE POSITIVE FOR METASTATIC ADENOCARCINOMA  THERE IS EXTENSIVE LYMPHATIC INVOLVEMENT WITHIN THE AXILLARY FAT  NOTE  At least four separate foci of carcinoma are identified in the breast parenchyma  including areas that did not show gross evidence of tumor  Examined inked margins are free of tumor  Because of the multifocal involvement  the absence of an in situ component  and the recent history of metastatic carcinoma elsewhere  we favor the interpretation that this tumor is a metastasis from the right breast primary  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 33 Consulting Pathologist s   Dennis Sgroi  M D  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a left modified radical mastectomy specimen weighing 445 grams  The total specimen measures 25 x 13 x 3 5cm  The breast measures 16 x 13 x 2 5cm and the axillary tail measures 9 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm  Overlying the specimen is a 17 x 6cm skin ellipse containing the nipple and a 4cm healed scar located inferolaterally to the nipple  Located deep to this scar is a hard nodular  white to yellow area with central hemorrhage  This nodular area measures 4 x 3 x 2cm  It extends to within 0 6cm of the deep margin and 1cm of the inferior margin  Located 7cm medially from the biopsy site and 4cm laterally from the medial resection margin is a 0 5cm hard  tan nodule  This nodule is 1 5cm beneath the skin surface and 2 5cm from the neasest resection margin which is the superior margin  Sectioning of the axillary fat reveals multiple lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 0 4cm  There are also two lymph nodes measuring REMOVED_DATE and the other 1 1cm  Section Code  A E representative sections from the biopsy cavity  F  section demonstrating the relationship of the biopsy site to the deep margin  G  representative sections demonstrating the relationship of the biopsy site to the inferior margin  H  representative sections of biopsy site with overlying skin  I J  the entire nodule from the medial lower quadrant  K  section from the upper medial quadrant  L  section from the medial lower quadrant  M  cystic structure from the outer lower quadrant  N O  nipple in its entirety  P S  axillary lymph nodes  T U  each contain a single large lymph node bisected  V  more axillary lymph nodes  Received separately labeled  Axillary lymph nodes  is a 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm fatty fragment of tissue bisected and submitted entirely  Resident  Lisa H  Lerner  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  Peter Hedberg  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , 11.
