Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 59 CLINICAL DATA  35 year old female  left core biopsy positive for infiltrating lobular carcinoma and lobular carcinoma in situ  Undergoes lumpectomy with needle localization with axillary lymph node dissection                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   LUMPECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  70   PRESENT AT AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN  SLIDE B  LEVELS EXAMINED  SEE NOTE  2  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  30    PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN  NOTE  The infiltrating component is present at the margin designated  deep medial    No vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  The tumor mass  in situ and invasive components  measures 1 2cm in maximal dimension  AXILLARY CONTENTS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN THIRTEEN OF THIRTEEN LYMPH NODES  0 13   Diagnosis by  Kathleen K  Hansen  MD Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 49                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 49 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm breast excision specimen  needle localizing in place and an accompanying X ray  Specimen is oriented by the surgeon  The lateral surface inked red  the inferior surface inked yellow  the medial surface inked green  and the superior surface inked black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal an ill defined 1 5cm stellate area extending to within 0 1cm of the deep margin closer to the medial side  A representative section of this area is frozen as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and submitted as A  Sections adjacent to the frozen section area on the deep margin in B through E  There is a 1 0cm  somewhat hemorrhagic tan area lateral to the stellate area  along the deep margin  representative section in F  The remaining specimen is tan yellow intermixed and focally rubbery with no definite masses  Representative section from the lateral margin in G  superior in H  medial in I  and inferior in J   Axillary dissection   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm piece of adipose tissue dissected to reveal greater than 10 nodules  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 2 0cm in greates