ors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 MAY 98 at 11 09 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   1   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 4cm portion of oriented breast tissue  A short suture designates the superficial margin  long and short sutures the inferior margin  and two long sutures the medial margin  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal a biopsy cavity with surrounding hard  white tissue  highly suspicious for tumor measuring 3 7cm in greatest dimension  radiating up to 0 8cm from the edge of the biopsy cavity  and approaching the superomedial and posteromedial margins  A second suspicious area  distant from the first area  measures 1 7cm in greatest dimension and approaches the superior margin of the specimen  SECTION CODE  A  Medial most section  B D  Closest superior margin  E F  Second lesion at superior margins  G   Representative section of superficial margin  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Part II   Final Inferior Margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm portion of breast tissue  which is inked black  The inferior and deep margins are over inked blue  which had been previously designated