 receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 28 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fibroadipose tissue fragment with a localization wire  The specimen is inked black and the lateral half is over inked green  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm ill defined  firm area abutting the posterolateral resection margin  A representative section of the firm area is frozen as FX  1  and resubmitted in A  The remaining firm area is submitted entirely in B E from superior to inferior  Additional representative sections are submitted in F H  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  new superior margin  suture on true margin    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue w