l assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 12 22 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm breast tissue  inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm ill defined white tan  stellate firm nodule  abutting the inked margin  A section of the nodule is frozen as FX 1 and resubmitted in A  The remaining nodule and neighboring tissue are submitted in B E  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Medial breast mass  right  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fragment of breast  inked and sectioned to reveal white fibrous tissue with no suspicious lesions  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes F through I  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Lateral breast mass  right side  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fragment of breast inked and sectioned to reveal tan yellow moderately firm tissue  grossly abutting the inked surface  submitted entirely in cassettes J through N  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  6 o clock  