ain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number only is an 805 gram modified radical mastectomy specimen  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm with an axillary tail REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE and overlying skin ellipse REMOVED_DATE x 8 0cm  At the central aspect of the inferior skin margin is a 2 5cm areola and nipple  and a healing scar is present 2 0cm in length extending to within 0 8cm to the superior margin and beginning 8 0cm from the medial margin of the skin ellipse  The specimen is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm biopsy cavity extending to within 0 7cm of the deep margin and to within 0 4cm of the superior margin  The remaining breast is unremarkable  Multiple lymph nodes are identified in the axillary tail  A 0 5cm  hard  well circumscribed nodule is identified 3 0cm deep to the nipple  Section code  A D  biopsy site with deep margin E  biopsy site with superior margin F J  representative breast tissue K  well circumscribed nodule L  nipple M O  axillary lymph nodes Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael L Grossbard  M D  PART   RIGHT MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , 1.
