 results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a 7 x 5 x 3 5cm fragment of breast tissue with a 5 x 1 5cm puckered skin ellipse on one side  The specimen is inked and sectioned to show a 4 x 2 x 1 5cm centrally yellow  gritty ill defined mass which extends to within 0 5cm of the inked margin  A representative section is frozen as FX  1 and saved as frozen   Representative sections of tumor in A through E  additional representative sections of uninvolved breast parenchyma in F through J  Frozen section in K  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axilla lymph node  is a 7 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm mass of fibroadipose tissue containing multiple palpable firm nodules  with two sutures attached at opposite ends  Sectioning into the tissue shows the presence of three large lymph nodes  the largest of which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm and several additional smaller lymph nodes  Representative sections of lymph nodes submitted in L through S  Resident  Robin E  Kirby  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                          