se tissue which is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm firm area which is sectioned to reveal a hemorrhagic cavity consistent with previous lymph node biopsy  The area shows yellow orange foci consistent with fat necrosis  Also noted are several tan pink lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 2 8cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Seven lymph nodes  in toto    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multiple lymph nodes  in toto    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multiple lymph nodes  in toto    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multiple lymph nodes  in toto    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Largest lymph node  bisected    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Hemorrhagic cavity  representative   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast lumpectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm yellow pink to white ovoid fibrofatty tissue  with a short stitch designating anterior  a long stitch designating lateral  and a bowtie designating cephalad  On the inferior and posterior aspects of the specimen  there are defects  communicating to a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm cavity  with a pink red hemorrhagic lining  The cavity also comes to within 0 1cm of the anterior margin  0 3cm to the lateral margin  and  1 5cm to the remaining two margins  The tissue surrounding the cavity varies from white and fibrotic to tan yellow and hemorrhagic  The remainder of the cut surface is yellow white and unremarkable  The specimen is inked as follows  superior green  inferior yellow  anterior blue  and posterior black  The specimen is submitted sequentially as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavity to anterior aspect   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavity to inferior defect   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavity to include area to posterior defect  Gross Dictation by Stephanie Kuehn  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Michael R Tan  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Kristina Braaten M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  Selected outside slides of the patient s prior right breast excision were reviewed  Newton Wellesley Hospital   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    These show an invasive poorly differentiated carcinoma with focal areas of ductal differentiation  adjacent ductal carcinoma in situ  extensive lymphatic invasion  and a positive sentinel lymph node  macrometastasis   These findings confirm the breast origin of the tumor identified in the current specimen  The majority of the tumor shows morphologic features of neuroendocrine differentiation  namely  solid nests of cells with high nuclear grade  finely granular chromatin without nucleoli  nuclear molding  high mitotic index   50 10 HPF   karyorrhectic debris  areas of spindling  and abundant necrosis  Together with the strongly positive chromogranin stain in the current material  the tumor is classified as invasive ductal carcinoma with large component of high grade neuroendocrine differentiated carcinoma  Addendum by Kristina Braaten M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   DISSECTION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION , 0.
