Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 00 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 17 02 CLINICAL DATA  78 year old female with known left breast cancer  extensive DCIS                                                                                       FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU WITH APOCRINE FEATURES  EXTENSIVE  FOCALLY INVOLVING A RADIAL SCAR AND SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  WITH A SMALL   0 4CM  AREA SUSPICIOUS BUT NOT DIAGNOSTIC FOR INVASION  SEE NOTE AND TABLE 1   TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS 1 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU Tumor size  Involving 7 of 14 blocks  spanning at least 4 0cm  Grade  2 Calcifications  Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  Margins of resection are free of carcinoma  NOTE  Periductal fibrosis  stromal reactive changes secondary to prior biopsy site  and focal involvement of sclerosing adenosis by in situ carcinoma make it difficult to accurately diagnosis microinvasive carcinoma in this case  The margins of resection are free of carcinoma  2 FOLLICULAR LYMPHOMA WITH SCLEROSIS  GRADE 1 OF 3  INVOLVING 4 OF 9 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE   NOTE  The lymphoma has an unusual appearance  some follicles are sclerotic and the lymphoid cells in them are spindled  resembling mesenchymal cells  Immunohistochemical studies will be performed and reported upon in an addendum  3 ALL  9  LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF BREAST CARCINOMA CELLS  4 RADIAL SCARS  5 FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH PROMINENT SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  6 BIOPSY CHANGES  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 16 45                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOPEROXIDASE STAINS  PARAFFIN SECTIONS OF AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  With antibody to B lineage antigen  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  there is staining of most cells in 