                        IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block O   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show moderate  2   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Breast  Left  block R   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 10 26 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 8 0cm irregular shaped skin ellipse  A stitch designates the 12 o clock position  The resection margin is inked in black and specimen is serially sectioned to reveal multiple cysts  the largest measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  There are two small papillomas  each REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  There are multiple coarse granular areas throughout the breast  A representative section of a granular area is frozen as FX 1  now submitted in cassette A  A representative section of the papillomas is submitted in cassette B  Representative sections of fibrous and granular breast tissue with association to the deep posterior margin are submitted in cassettes C J  from medial to lateral  The axillary tissue is examined for lymph nodes  and there are six lymph nodes which are submitted in cassette K  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left MRM   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm breast with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axilla  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 7 5cm skin ellipse with an unremarkable 1 0cm everted nipple  The posterior aspect of the specimen is inked in black  and serially sectioned to reveal an ill defined  gritty  tan white area of firm and fibrous breast parenchyma which measures approximately 5 0cm in greatest dimension and is located 0 5cm from deep margin  and more than 4 0cm from superior  more than 6 0cm from inferior  more than 5 0cm from medial  and more than 13cm from lateral margins  There is a separate stellate lesion with tan white color and a chalky punctate surface  which measures approximately 1 5cm in diameter and is located 1 0cm from deep margin  the closest margin   Inferiorly  there is an additional tan yellow firm well circumscribed lobulated nodule  measuring 0 7cm in diameter  located 0 7cm from deep margin  The rest of the specimen is grossly unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  The axillary tail is examined for lymph nodes  L Q  Ill defined mass with deep resection margin  R S  Stellate lesion  T  Inferior lobulated nodule  U  Parenchyma  V X  Whole lymph nodes  Resident  ALIREZA SEPEHR  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  NORMA RODRIGUEZ  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                               