f estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 07 13 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm lumpectomy specimen with long stitch designating lateral and short stitch designating superior  The specimen contains an overlying skin ellipse that measures REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  with a 2 5cm linear  healed incision  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 2cm in greatest dimension  ill defined area of firm  tan tissue with a central gray  necrotic area  that extends to within 0 5cm of the overlying skin ellipse and 4 0cm of the deep margin  The surrounding breast parenchyma is tan white to yellow and rubbery  No other lesions are grossly identified  A frozen was done of the suspicious area and saved frozen  SECTION CODE  A  necrotic focus with deep resection margin  representative section  B  necrotic focus with inferior r