CISION  BREAST PARENCHYMA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  LEFT  SUPERIOR FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISION  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  LEFT  LATERAL FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISION  BREAST PARENCHYMA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA CONTENTS   EXCISION  ALL EIGHT  8  LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  LYMPH NODE  ADDITIONAL  LEFT AXILLA CONTENTS   EXCISION  TWO LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  See note   NOTE  Immunostains are negative for keratin positive tumor cells  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm breast excision specimen  with a long stitch indicating lateral  a short stitch superior  and a needle localization wire embedded within the tissue  The superior  inferior  anterior  lateral  and medial surfaces display a pink orange  shiny  lobular  unremarkable surface  The posterior surface is tan pink  shaggy and fibrous  Correlation with the attached mammogram reveals a metal clip within the central portion of the specimen  as well as a small central area of probable calcification  The specimen is inked per protocol with respect to the medial lateral long axis  as follows  anterior   blue  posterior   black  superior   green  inferior   yellow  Serial sectioning perpendicular to the long axis reveals two areas of hemorrhage consistent with prior recent biopsy  Both areas measure 0 8cm in greatest dimension  The first area of hemorrhage is adjacent to the posterior margin  and the second is located centrally  The metal clip is identified adjacent to the central hemorrhagic area  The tissue surrounding the central area of hemorrhage is tan gray and shiny  with a few small areas of tan firmness surrounding  No discrete masses or lesions are identified  The specimen is submitted entirely from medial to lateral in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with the section containing the slightly firmer tissue adjacent to the central hemorrhage in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and the section containing the metal clip in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    M J   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  inferior final shaved margins   are multiple fragments of tan pink  shaggy to shiny soft tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm in aggregate  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a tan pink  unremarkable cut surface  and is submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  medial final shaved margins   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of tan pink to yellow  unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  sectioned and submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  superior final shaved margins   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of pink brown  shiny to shaggy  unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  lateral shaved final margins   are two fragments of tan brown to pink  shiny to shaggy  unremarkable fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm in aggregate  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary contents   are two fragments of red orange  shiny fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm in aggregate  Nine candidate lymph nodes ranging in greatest dimension from 0 2cm to 1 2cm  are identified  The candidate lymph nodes are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Five candidate lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Four candidate lymph nodes  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional left axilla contents   are multiple fragments of tan yellow  fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm in aggregate  Two lymph nodes  measuring REMOVED_DATE and 1 3cm in greatest dimension respectively  are identified  The specimen is submitted entirely as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Attached fibroadipose tissue  Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT  INFERIOR FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT  MEDIAL FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISION PART D  BREAST  LEFT  SUPERIOR FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISION PART E  BREAST  LEFT  LATERAL FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISION PART F  LYMPH NODE  LEFT A  report_end  , 0.
