osite surface  adjacent to the previous specimen is inked blue  Sectioning through the specimen reveals at least three  white firm and spiculated areas  one closest to the superomedial end  abutting the superior  new  resection margin  measuring 1 5cm in maximal diameter  A separate area of firmness  measuring 0 5cm in maximal diameter is located in the deep portion of the specimen  adjacent to the superior  new  resection margin  A third irregular area of white  firm tissue is located near the inferolateral resection margin  closest to the deep resection margin  blue ink   Section code  I O  representative sections  from superomedial to inferolateral with first area of firmness in I and J  intermediate area of firmness in K through M  and inferolateral area of firmness in N and O  Labeled  left axillary lymph nodes  Level I  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm mass of adipose and fibrous tissue  Lymph nodes are dissected and submitted in P through S  Labeled  left axillary lymph nodes  Level II  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm aggregate of adipose tissue  containing few lymph nodes  Submitted entirely in T and U  labeled  left axilla  hot spot  1  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm aggregate of adipose tissue  containing at least one large lymph node  Dissected and submitted entirely in V through X  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT  SPECIMEN  1  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  LEFT   ADDITIONAL MARGIN PART C  LYMPH NODES  LEVEL 1  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION PART D  LYMPH NODES  LEVEL II  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION PART E  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY HOT SPOT   EXCISION   report_end  , 0.
