lts of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 MAY 95 at 08 22 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  are two fragments of breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm  The longer fragment contains a needle guide wire and is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm irregular well demarcated firm nodule with infiltrative borders  the nodule abuts the ink  A representative section is frozen as FX 1  Frozen section is saved and sent to Cox 5  Remainder of longer specimen is entirely submitted in A through F  nodule in B through E  The smaller fragment is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm irregular well demarcated yellow firm nodule with infiltrative borders grossly abutting the ink  No frozen is done  submitted entirely in G through H  Resident  SCOTT D  URBAN  HMS     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST LEFT  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  RICHARD S  HAMILTON  HMS O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Keith Thomas Paige M D  Peter