cision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 08 05 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast lumpectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fragment of fibrofatty breast tissue  with a long stitch marking lateral and a short stitch marking superior  The superior aspect is inked black  the inferior aspect blue  and the posterior aspect overinked green  The specimen is serially sectioned medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE firm white  ill defined mass  which grossly appears to abut the inferior deep margin  It is 1 0mm from the closest superior margin  A representative section of the inferior margin in relation to the tumor is frozen as FX 2  Adjacent to the stellate mass is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm white fibrous thickening abutting the inferior margin  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel node right axilla   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan pink fragment of soft tissue  which is entirely frozen as FX 1  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast final shaving   are 8 fragments of yellow pink fibroadipose tissue  which range in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  The unoriented fragments are inked black and serially sectioned to reveal no gross abnormalities  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm unoriented piece of adipose tissue  The specimen is dissected for lymph nodes  several of which are found ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  SECTION CODE  A   FX 2  Inferior margin and tumor  B   Tumor  lateral most section  including posterior superior inferior margin  C D  Sections of tumor and closest anterior posterior margin bisected  entirely submitted  E J  Area of thickening  inferior  anterior margin K   Representative section away from tumor  L   FX 1  Sentinel lymph node  M R  Final shaved margin  entirely submitted  S BB lymph nodes  submitted in toto with one bisected node in Z  Resident  PAULA ARNELL  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  SENTINEL NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   ADIPOSE TISSUE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF LYMPH NODE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2 INFERIOR MARGIN OF  RIGHT BREAST MASS   MARGIN NEGATIVE  TUMOR APPROXIMATELY REMOVED_DATE CM FROM MARGIN  O R  Resident  LISA A  GALLAGHER  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  Simon Powell  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   FINAL SHAVE    RE EXCISION PART C  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA     SENTINEL    EXCISION PART D  BREAST RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , 0.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 19 13 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 2 3   EXTENDING TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE INKED DEEP RESECTION MARGIN  AND WITH BLOOD VASCULAR  VENOUS  INVASION   SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INTERMEDIATE TO HIGH PRESENT IN 5 OF 5 SLIDES  EXTENDING TO THE INKED DEEP RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE   3  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 20 OF 20 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Several foci are highly suspicious for lymphatic invasion  Dr  Koerner agrees with the interpretation of blood vascular invasion  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 18 12                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 21 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast and axillary dissection  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm mastectomy with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm skin ellipse with an unremarkable 1 5cm nipple  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm axillary tail is attached to the main specimen  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm firm  tan white stellate nodule extending to approximately REMOVED_DATE to 0 2cm of the deep resection margin  Further sectioning reveals the remainder of the breast to be composed of predominantly fibrous  tan rubbery tissue intermixed with unremarkable adipose tissue  A representative section of the firm mass and deep resection margin is submitted in cassette A  Representative sections of the remainder of the mass are submitted in cassettes B through E  Representative sections of unremarkable parenchyma are submitted entirely in cassette F  The axillary tail is sectioned to reveal multiple rubbery tan pink lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 2 0cm  The lymph nodes are submitted entirely in cassettes G through M  The nipple is trisected and submitted entirely in cassette N  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  AMBULATORY GEN SURG   ACC 457 REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT  and AXILLARY CONTENTS   report_end  , 0.
