ptor  Negative  progesterone receptor  Negative  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 27     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 08 05 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a 4 x 2 x 1cm piece of firm  white yellow breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal firm  white tissue and yellow fat  Representative section is frozen as FX 1 and kept frozen  The remainder is submitted entirely in A and B  Received fresh later  is a  REMOVED_CASE_ID  gram  partial mastectomy specimen consisting of 15 x 12cm black skin with underlying 21 x 14 x 11cm firm  white yellow tissue and attached 7 x 4 x 3cm piece of axillary adipose tissue  Two sutures are present on the skin  The longer one designates lateral and the short one designates the superior margin  The external surface of the skin is remarkable for a 15 x 11cm bulging white yellow  friable mass with a 6 x 2cm central ulceration which is 4cm deep within the breast parenchyma  The mass is within less than 0 5cm of the lateral skin resection margins  at multiple foci both superiorly and inferiorly  2cm from the lateral axillary skin resection margin and 2 5cm from the medial skin resection margin  The nipple is not identifiable but a pin is present designated by the surgeon as nipple remnant  Further sectioning reveals entire involvement of the breast by firm  white yellow  focally friable tissue  The mass measures 11 x 6 x 13cm beneath the skin and extends to the inked deep soft tissue margins as well as superior inferior soft tissue margins  Also present is REMOVED_DATE x 4 x 4cm piece of red tan skeletal muscle superiorly adjacent to the axillary adipose tissue  The mass appears to infiltrate the skeletal muscle in a nodular fashion  The axillary adipose tissue contains several lymph nodes with white tan  solid cut surfaces  the largest 1 2cm in greatest diameter  Section Code  C  skin ends from both lateral and medial resection margins  D  inked deep soft tissue margins  E  tumor and skin from superior edge  F  tumor and skin from inferior edge  G  nipple remnant and representative junction of skin with tumor  H J  more representative tumor  K  lymph nodes  L  representative skeletal muscle  M  designated nipple remnant  Resident  Metin Ozdemirli  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST RIGHT BIOPSY   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Debra F Weinstein  M D  Kimberly S Kirkwood  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS