dings are compatible with healing biopsy site with exuberant granulation tissue and no evidence of malignancy  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 3 containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received in formalin and labeled  lateral margin left breast  stitch marks new margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm fragment of fibrofatty breast tissue  with a stitch marking the new margin  The new margin is inked black  The surface opposite the new margin is focally hemorrhagic and shows red brown granulation tissue focally  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal indurated fatty tissue  with foci of fat necrosis adjacent to the margin opposite the new margin  Submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin and labeled  anterior margin left breast  stitch marks new margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fragment of fibrofatty breast tissue  with a stitch marking the new margin  The margin opposite the new margin shows red brown granulation tissue  with foci of fat necrosis and indurated fatty tissue  The new margin is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin and labeled  left axillary lymph node contents   is a fragment of fibrofatty axillary tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 8cm  which on dissection shows several tan pink and tan gray lymph nodes  measuring from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm  The larger lymph nodes are serially sectioned  Most of the larger lymph nodes are partially replaced by fatty tissue  The axillary fibrofatty tissue also shows a tan red cavity  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The cavity is surrounded by indurated fatty tissue  with foci of fat necrosis and hemorrhage  This may represent the previous biopsy site of a possible sentinel lymph node  All the lymph nodes and possible lymph nodes are entirely submitted  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Largest lymph node  serially sectioned and entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2nd largest possible lymph node  serially sectioned and entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   3rd largest lymph node  serially sectioned and entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   4th largest lymph node  serially sectioned and entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Next 4 larger lymph nodes  each serially sectioned and entirely but separately submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remaining smaller lymph nodes and candidate lymph nodes  entirely submitted in toto   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavity with surrounding indurated fatty tissue  with foci of hemorrhage and fat necrosis  Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on Monday REMOVED_MONTH 05   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 03 21 09PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Breast  Left lateral Margin   Excision PART B  Breast  Left anterior Margin   Excision PART C  Lymph Nodes  Left Axilla   Dissection  report_end  , 0.
