breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 01 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast short stitch superior  long lateral  is a 38 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm right breast lumpectomy specimen oriented with superior and lateral stitches  The specimen is partially covered by a REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm skin ellipse with a central 2 8cm well healed scar running along the long axis of the ellipse  there is no areola  There is no axillary tail on the specimen  The deep resection margin is a smooth plain  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a prior REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm cystic biopsy cavity filled with red tan groumous material  and surrounded by a rim of intense fibrosis and semi firm sulphur yellow discoloration  The biopsy site is inferior to the skin ellipse  and abuts the inferior resection margin  The biopsy site comes to within 0 1cm of the superior margin  0 4cm of the deep inked margin  0 6cm of the lateral margin  and 1 5cm of the medial margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma consists of mature  lobular  yellow  adipose tissue with intercolating fibrous bands  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right axillary contents  is a 36 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of tan yellow  lobulated  fibroadipose tissue which is explored for lymph nodes  Lymph nodes are identified  Summary of sections  A G  Biopsy site with skin  superior  in yellow   in