Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 09 35 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  REMOVED_DATE CM  INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free of tumor  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 12 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor is confined to the lymph node  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 59                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 57 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast with axillary contents  is a 19 x 15 x 6cm left mastectomy specimen with an 11 x 9 x 2 5cm attached axillary tail  There is an overlying 16 x 8cm skin ellipse with an eccentric  unremarkable nipple areola complex  There are no evident scars on the skin surface  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm firm  stellate  tan white tumor located 0 5cm from the closest deep margin and 0 9cm from the closest anterior margin  Adjacent to this mass is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm rubbery area of fibrous tissue  The remaining parenchyma is interspersed with moderate amounts of dense white fibrous tissue with no additional anomalies  SECTION CODE A C  Tumor in its entirety in relation to closest deep margin  D  Lesion with adjacent fibrous area  E  Representative of unremarkable fibrous tissue from lateral aspect  F  Fibrous tissue from central aspect  G  Fibrous tissue from medial aspect  There are two ill defined  firm areas of fibrous parenchyma in the posteromedial aspect which are submitted in cassette H  Sectioning through the axillary tag reveals multiple  pink gray lymph nodes measuring up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  Representative sections of each lymph node are submitted in cassettes I through K  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Arlan F Fuller Jr   M D  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY , 1.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  28 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  28 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 19 08 CLINICAL DATA  Approximately nine month history of right breast mass  biopsy positive for malignancy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION     INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE SEE NOTE  1  NOTE  1  All of the resection margins are negative  infiltrating ductal carcinoma extends to within 0 5cm of the closest margin     SCAR  BREAST  RIGHT TISSUE   EXCISION     INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  95   REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  SEE NOTE  2  NOTE  2  All of the resection margins are negative  however  infiltrating ductal carcinoma extends to within 0 1cm of the closest resection margin     DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU 5  SOLID TYPE  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY CONTENTS      METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA  2 5 CM DIAMETER  TO 1 OF 14 LYMPH NODES  EXTRACAPSULAR EXTENSION IS PRESENT  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 19 03 Consulting Pathologist s   Michael Pins  M D  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast re excision  is a 7 x 5 x 2cm right lumpectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm horizontal skin ellipse  A 2 2cm well healed longitudinal central scar is present within the skin ellipse  The specimen is oriented by a long stitch laterally  and a short stitch superiorly  The semifirm  yellow  fibrofatty tissue is inked yellow  laterally  and black medially  Specimen is serially sectioned  revealing fibrofatty breast tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm white  firm area  grossly abutting the anterior  medially  black inked margin  Located within the superior and inferior aspects of the sample are two biopsy cavities measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  respectively  Section Code A B   closest margins of tumor  mid anterior medial C D   representative sections of lateral breast with skin E   representative section of medial breast with biopsy cavity F   representative section of medial breast G   representative section of breast superior aspect  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  H   breast  representative sections of inferior margin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  I   representative section of breast  deep margin Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  add breast tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 0 8cm piece of soft  red tan breast tissue  oriented by a long stitch laterally and a short stitch on the new inferior margin  The specimen is inked yellow laterally  and black medially and serially sectioned to reveal fibrous tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm well circumscribed white  firm nodule within 2mm of the upper anterior superior portion  Section Code J   closest margin  upper anterior superior portion K L   remaining tissue submitted from inferior to superior Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right axillary contents  is a 7 x 5 x 1 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue which contains multiple lymph nodes  including a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm hard  white collection of matted lymph nodes  Cross sectioning of this mass reveals firm  white tissue with a lobulated appearance  Section Code M N O   axillary lymph nodes  measuring from REMOVED_DATE to 0 4cm in diameter P   representative section of large matted lymph nodes Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT TISSUE   EXCISION PART C  RIGHT AXILLARY CONTENTS   report_end  , 1.
